meta {
  name: Screen - Reply
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/me/screen/reply
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "text": "I read fairly slowly, especially long paragraphs. I sometimes need to re-read sentences.",
    "session_id": "{{session_id}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.session_id: isDefined
  res.body.is_complete: isDefined
}

docs {
  Submit a reply for the current screening question. Run this 15+ times to walk
  through the full Adult Dyslexia Checklist. `is_complete` flips to true on the
  final turn.

  On completion the server runs a SECOND LLM call (post-process callback) that
  maps each answer to a checklist column and computes the weighted result. It is
  returned in `ahrq_result` (and persisted to `feature_history.metadata`).

  Expected `ahrq_result` shape on success:
    {
      "ahrq_status": "success",
      "ahrq_started_at": "2026-07-03T12:34:56Z",
      "ahrq_finished_at": "2026-07-03T12:35:12Z",
      "ahrq_error": null,
      "ahrq_scores": [2, 3, 1, ...],           // 15 ints, chosen column 0-4 (0 = unanswered)
      "ahrq_comments": "slow reader;heavy,...", // comma-sep, index-aligned
      "ahrq_total": 45,                        // weighted, range 22-88
      "ahrq_max_total": 88,
      "ahrq_severity": "unlikely" | "mild" | "moderate_severe", // <45 | 45-60 | >60
      "ahrq_disclaimer": "...",                // always display
      "ahrq_attribution": "© Ian Smythe & John Everatt, 2001."
    }

  On failure (LLM refused, malformed JSON, schema mismatch, etc.):
    {
      "ahrq_status": "failed",
      "ahrq_error": { "reason": "...", "message": "..." },
      "ahrq_scores": null,
      ...
    }
  The `/reply` call still returns 200 — the warm summary is unaffected.

  To re-run post-processing later (e.g. after a failed result), call
  `POST /api/v1/me/screen/{session_id}/postprocess` — see "Postprocess (re-run)".
  Commas inside a comment are sanitized to ';' (not a failure).
}
